## 2. Test Objectives

The purpose of these tests was to verify the fundamental operating functions of the conveyor control program under simulated conditions.

The validation covered normal stopping, simulated fault response, individual product counting, automatic cycle completion, and counter reset.

## 3. Test Results

| Test ID | Test Description | Expected Result | Reported Result | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| TC-01 | Normal Stop | Motor command and output turn OFF when the stop condition is activated. | Expected stopping behavior observed. | PASS |
| TC-02 | Simulated Fault | Motor command and output turn OFF when a simulated fault is activated. | Expected fault response observed. | PASS |
| TC-03 | Individual Product Counting | Each valid rising edge from the product sensor increments the counter by one. | Individual product counting verified. | PASS |
| TC-04 | Automatic Cycle Completion | The conveyor stops when the product counter reaches the preset value of five. | Cycle completion behavior observed. | PASS |
| TC-05 | Counter Reset | The product counter returns to zero when the reset command is activated. | Counter reset verified. | PASS |

## 4. Functional Verification Summary

All five reported functional tests passed in the S7-PLCSIM simulation environment.

The reported results support the following conclusions:

- The normal stop condition disables the conveyor motor command.
- The simulated fault condition disables the conveyor motor command.
- Product counting uses individual sensor detections rather than continuously counting a sustained sensor signal.
- The automatic cycle terminates when the preset production quantity is reached.
- The counter can be reset for a subsequent test cycle.

## 5. Test Limitations

These results apply to the simulated PLC program and the tested operating conditions.

The tests do not establish the performance of a physical conveyor, motor starter, field wiring, real sensors, or safety-related hardware. Further validation would be required before deployment in an industrial installation.

## 6. Recommended Next Tests

The following tests are recommended to improve the completeness of the validation:

- Verify that the motor cannot restart unexpectedly after a stop or fault condition is cleared.
- Verify that a new automatic cycle requires a deliberate start command.
- Verify that manual and automatic modes cannot command the motor simultaneously.
- Verify that reset behavior is correct when a fault is active.
- Verify sensor behavior during rapid transitions and prolonged activation.
- Verify startup behavior and counter initialization after a PLC restart.

## 7. Conclusion

The conveyor control program completed all five reported functional tests in simulation.

This project demonstrates practical experience with Siemens PLC programming, Ladder Logic, digital input/output handling, edge detection, counter instructions, operating conditions, fault response, and functional test documentation.

**Project status:** Functional simulation tests completed. Additional robustness testing and technical documentation are recommended before considering the design complete.

